1
00:00:00,519 --> 00:00:01,933
There's a lot of advice out there

2
00:00:01,772 --> 00:00:02,770
about cats.

3
00:00:03,129 --> 00:00:04,203
Some of it is great.

4
00:00:04,541 --> 00:00:06,439
And some of it has been wrong

5
00:00:06,495 --> 00:00:07,969
for hundreds of years.

6
00:00:08,949 --> 00:00:12,046
Millions of people still believe things about

7
00:00:11,948 --> 00:00:14,867
cats that science has already proved false,

8
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:17,498
and some of those myths can actually

9
00:00:17,368 --> 00:00:18,353
hurt your cat.

10
00:00:19,358 --> 00:00:21,468
So today, we're busting twelve of the

11
00:00:21,310 --> 00:00:24,098
most common cat myths, one by one,

12
00:00:24,289 --> 00:00:26,244
and finding out what's really true.

13
00:00:27,265 --> 00:00:28,093
Myth number one:

14
00:00:28,506 --> 00:00:29,599
cats need milk.

15
00:00:29,918 --> 00:00:32,695
It's the classic cartoon image, a happy

16
00:00:32,610 --> 00:00:34,438
cat lapping up a bowl of milk.

17
00:00:35,418 --> 00:00:36,128
The truth:

18
00:00:36,484 --> 00:00:39,481
most adult cats are lactose intolerant.

19
00:00:39,796 --> 00:00:42,454
As kittens grow up, many lose the

20
00:00:42,312 --> 00:00:44,906
ability to properly digest the sugar in

21
00:00:44,796 --> 00:00:45,309
milk.

22
00:00:46,312 --> 00:00:48,108
So that bowl of milk can lead

23
00:00:47,962 --> 00:00:51,274
to an upset stomach, gas or diarrhea.

24
00:00:51,618 --> 00:00:53,857
Not exactly the treat we imagined.

25
00:00:54,825 --> 00:00:57,545
Kittens drink their mother's milk, of course,

26
00:00:57,431 --> 00:01:00,121
but after weaning, what cats really need

27
00:00:59,999 --> 00:01:02,083
is fresh, clean water.

28
00:01:03,069 --> 00:01:05,289
If your cat really loves milk, there

29
00:01:05,116 --> 00:01:08,238
are special lactose-free milks made for cats.

30
00:01:08,591 --> 00:01:10,741
But even those should only be an

31
00:01:10,587 --> 00:01:11,754
occasional treat.

32
00:01:12,723 --> 00:01:13,740
Myth number two:

33
00:01:14,219 --> 00:01:16,898
cats always land on their feet, so

34
00:01:16,786 --> 00:01:18,036
falls can't hurt them.

35
00:01:18,331 --> 00:01:20,465
It's true that cats have an amazing

36
00:01:20,349 --> 00:01:23,489
righting reflex, and can twist in mid-air.

37
00:01:24,458 --> 00:01:26,370
But they need time and height to

38
00:01:26,238 --> 00:01:27,090
turn around.

39
00:01:27,401 --> 00:01:29,661
From a very short fall, they may

40
00:01:29,542 --> 00:01:31,043
not have time to twist.

41
00:01:32,058 --> 00:01:34,413
And from high places, landing on their

42
00:01:34,286 --> 00:01:36,343
feet doesn't stop injuries.

43
00:01:36,669 --> 00:01:39,746
Vets treat many cats every year after

44
00:01:39,611 --> 00:01:41,808
falls from windows and balconies.

45
00:01:42,805 --> 00:01:44,471
Cats don't have nine lives.

46
00:01:44,816 --> 00:01:46,680
If you live in an apartment, window

47
00:01:46,568 --> 00:01:48,614
screens are one of the best gifts

48
00:01:48,458 --> 00:01:49,536
you can give your cat.

49
00:01:50,640 --> 00:01:51,557
Fun fact:

50
00:01:51,922 --> 00:01:54,818
the nine lives idea changes around the

51
00:01:54,672 --> 00:01:55,228
world.

52
00:01:55,530 --> 00:01:58,540
In Spanish-speaking countries, cats are said to

53
00:01:58,401 --> 00:02:01,562
have seven lives, and in some places,

54
00:02:01,910 --> 00:02:02,909
only six.

55
00:02:03,926 --> 00:02:05,062
Myth number three:

56
00:02:05,453 --> 00:02:08,127
a purring cat is always a happy

57
00:02:08,062 --> 00:02:08,586
cat.

58
00:02:08,939 --> 00:02:11,497
Most of the time, purring does mean

59
00:02:11,392 --> 00:02:12,311
contentment.

60
00:02:13,308 --> 00:02:15,733
But cats also purr when they're stressed,

61
00:02:15,892 --> 00:02:19,475
injured, giving birth, or even very sick.

62
00:02:19,824 --> 00:02:22,665
Scientists think purring may help them calm

63
00:02:22,576 --> 00:02:24,219
down and feel better.

64
00:02:25,212 --> 00:02:26,931
So always look at the whole picture.

65
00:02:27,254 --> 00:02:30,277
A purring cat that's hiding, not eating

66
00:02:30,177 --> 00:02:33,135
or breathing strangely needs a vet, not

67
00:02:33,025 --> 00:02:33,843
just a cuddle.

68
00:02:34,842 --> 00:02:38,291
Some researchers even think the low frequencies

69
00:02:38,152 --> 00:02:41,235
of purring might help bones and tissues

70
00:02:41,141 --> 00:02:41,654
heal.

71
00:02:41,964 --> 00:02:44,710
It's a fascinating idea, but it still

72
00:02:44,584 --> 00:02:46,413
needs more research.

73
00:02:47,386 --> 00:02:48,359
Myth number four:

74
00:02:48,791 --> 00:02:50,984
cats are cold and don't really love

75
00:02:50,841 --> 00:02:51,725
their owners.

76
00:02:52,036 --> 00:02:54,200
This might be the most unfair myth

77
00:02:54,072 --> 00:02:54,680
of all.

78
00:02:55,648 --> 00:02:59,391
In a 2019 study, researchers tested cats

79
00:02:59,287 --> 00:03:01,736
with a classic attachment test used for

80
00:03:01,611 --> 00:03:02,860
babies and dogs.

81
00:03:03,883 --> 00:03:06,237
Most of the cats showed a secure

82
00:03:06,115 --> 00:03:08,054
attachment to their owners.

83
00:03:08,355 --> 00:03:11,277
They felt safer and more confident when

84
00:03:11,105 --> 00:03:12,497
their person was in the room.

85
00:03:13,507 --> 00:03:16,122
Cats just show love in quieter ways:

86
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:20,492
slow blinks, head bumps, following you around,

87
00:03:20,857 --> 00:03:22,449
and choosing to be near you.

88
00:03:23,425 --> 00:03:24,176
And remember:

89
00:03:24,622 --> 00:03:27,460
adult cats rarely meow at other cats,

90
00:03:27,604 --> 00:03:29,430
but they meow at us all the

91
00:03:29,296 --> 00:03:29,809
time.

92
00:03:30,133 --> 00:03:32,350
That sound is basically made for you.

93
00:03:33,356 --> 00:03:34,577
So if your cat greets you at

94
00:03:34,410 --> 00:03:37,244
the door, sleeps on your clothes, or

95
00:03:37,095 --> 00:03:39,768
brings you a gift, that's love, cat

96
00:03:39,691 --> 00:03:40,368
style.

97
00:03:41,321 --> 00:03:42,327
Myth number five:

98
00:03:42,801 --> 00:03:44,319
cats are nocturnal.

99
00:03:44,628 --> 00:03:45,587
Not exactly.

100
00:03:45,923 --> 00:03:48,515
Cats are crepuscular, which means they're most

101
00:03:48,509 --> 00:03:50,589
active at dawn and dusk.

102
00:03:51,593 --> 00:03:54,302
That's when their wild ancestors hunted small

103
00:03:54,198 --> 00:03:54,783
prey.

104
00:03:55,096 --> 00:03:56,956
It's why your cat suddenly gets the

105
00:03:56,829 --> 00:03:59,945
zoomies at sunrise, or right when you

106
00:03:59,773 --> 00:04:01,079
want to relax in the evening.

107
00:04:02,065 --> 00:04:03,953
A good play session in the evening

108
00:04:03,917 --> 00:04:05,938
can help your cat use that energy

109
00:04:05,824 --> 00:04:08,828
before bedtime, instead of at five in

110
00:04:08,648 --> 00:04:09,310
the morning.

111
00:04:10,304 --> 00:04:12,552
Feeding a meal right after that play

112
00:04:12,416 --> 00:04:13,671
session helps too.

113
00:04:14,033 --> 00:04:16,470
Hunt, eat, groom, sleep:

114
00:04:16,682 --> 00:04:18,475
that's the natural cat routine.

115
00:04:19,460 --> 00:04:20,635
Myth number six:

116
00:04:21,044 --> 00:04:23,394
cats can see in complete darkness.

117
00:04:23,715 --> 00:04:26,023
Cats do have amazing night vision.

118
00:04:26,312 --> 00:04:28,112
They can see in light about six

119
00:04:28,013 --> 00:04:29,674
times dimmer than we need.

120
00:04:30,658 --> 00:04:33,099
But in total darkness, with no light

121
00:04:32,957 --> 00:04:35,181
at all, cats can't see either.

122
00:04:35,473 --> 00:04:38,768
They rely on their whiskers, ears and

123
00:04:38,656 --> 00:04:39,967
nose to get around.

124
00:04:41,007 --> 00:04:43,539
So a tiny night light can actually

125
00:04:43,384 --> 00:04:45,388
help an older cat find its way

126
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:46,657
to the litter box at night.

127
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:50,082
Their eyes also glow in the dark,

128
00:04:50,273 --> 00:04:52,712
thanks to a mirror-like layer that reflects

129
00:04:52,603 --> 00:04:53,181
light.

130
00:04:53,512 --> 00:04:55,569
That glow is part of why people

131
00:04:55,429 --> 00:04:58,023
thought cats had magic night vision.

132
00:04:58,986 --> 00:04:59,994
Myth number seven:

133
00:05:00,350 --> 00:05:01,796
all cats hate water.

134
00:05:02,097 --> 00:05:04,687
Many cats don't like getting soaked, partly

135
00:05:04,548 --> 00:05:06,957
because wet fur gets heavy and takes

136
00:05:06,804 --> 00:05:08,132
a long time to dry.

137
00:05:09,160 --> 00:05:10,882
But some cats love water.

138
00:05:11,202 --> 00:05:13,817
Breeds like the Turkish Van are famous

139
00:05:13,696 --> 00:05:16,817
for swimming, and many cats love playing

140
00:05:16,660 --> 00:05:17,819
with a dripping tap.

141
00:05:18,839 --> 00:05:20,784
So it's not that cats hate water.

142
00:05:21,106 --> 00:05:23,420
Most cats just hate being forced into

143
00:05:23,311 --> 00:05:23,594
it.

144
00:05:24,576 --> 00:05:25,800
If you ever need to bathe your

145
00:05:25,684 --> 00:05:28,984
cat, use lukewarm water, keep it short

146
00:05:28,938 --> 00:05:31,300
and calm, and dry your cat well

147
00:05:31,143 --> 00:05:32,638
with a towel afterwards.

148
00:05:33,604 --> 00:05:34,540
Myth number eight:

149
00:05:34,892 --> 00:05:36,183
cats can't be trained.

150
00:05:36,482 --> 00:05:37,745
Actually, they can.

151
00:05:38,088 --> 00:05:39,847
They just don't work for praise the

152
00:05:39,707 --> 00:05:40,726
way dogs do.

153
00:05:41,727 --> 00:05:44,560
With treats and patience, cats can learn

154
00:05:44,392 --> 00:05:48,057
to come when called, sit, high-five, and

155
00:05:47,923 --> 00:05:49,473
even walk on a harness.

156
00:05:50,418 --> 00:05:53,385
A 2019 study in Japan also found

157
00:05:53,234 --> 00:05:56,032
that cats can recognize their own names.

158
00:05:56,381 --> 00:05:58,050
They just choose when to answer.

159
00:05:59,030 --> 00:06:01,635
The secret is positive reinforcement:

160
00:06:02,080 --> 00:06:04,174
reward what you like, and never punish.

161
00:06:04,511 --> 00:06:06,881
Short, fun sessions work best.

162
00:06:07,868 --> 00:06:10,456
Training also keeps your cat's brain busy,

163
00:06:10,657 --> 00:06:12,238
and it can make vet visits and

164
00:06:12,081 --> 00:06:14,770
carrier trips much less stressful.

165
00:06:15,739 --> 00:06:18,423
Start with something easy, like rewarding your

166
00:06:18,306 --> 00:06:20,066
cat for coming to you when you

167
00:06:19,927 --> 00:06:21,152
shake the treat bag.

168
00:06:21,485 --> 00:06:23,950
Many cats learn that one very quickly.

169
00:06:24,934 --> 00:06:25,818
Myth number nine:

170
00:06:26,189 --> 00:06:27,865
black cats are bad luck.

171
00:06:28,184 --> 00:06:30,924
This superstition comes from the Middle Ages,

172
00:06:31,081 --> 00:06:33,764
when black cats were wrongly linked to

173
00:06:33,635 --> 00:06:34,610
witchcraft.

174
00:06:35,575 --> 00:06:38,083
But in many places, it's the opposite.

175
00:06:38,397 --> 00:06:41,132
In Britain and Japan, a black cat

176
00:06:41,192 --> 00:06:43,330
is traditionally seen as a sign of

177
00:06:43,167 --> 00:06:43,866
good luck.

178
00:06:44,809 --> 00:06:46,244
And the truth is simple:

179
00:06:46,610 --> 00:06:48,527
a black cat is just a cat,

180
00:06:48,827 --> 00:06:51,919
with the same personality, the same love,

181
00:06:52,237 --> 00:06:54,554
and the same amazing senses.

182
00:06:55,570 --> 00:06:58,731
Some shelters even say black cats can

183
00:06:58,624 --> 00:07:01,523
wait longer to be adopted, partly because

184
00:07:01,365 --> 00:07:03,353
they're harder to photograph.

185
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:05,789
So if you're adopting, give the black

186
00:07:05,667 --> 00:07:06,826
cats a chance.

187
00:07:07,791 --> 00:07:08,814
Myth number ten:

188
00:07:09,248 --> 00:07:11,822
indoor cats don't need exercise.

189
00:07:12,163 --> 00:07:15,550
Indoor cats live longer and safer lives,

190
00:07:15,699 --> 00:07:17,622
but they still have the body and

191
00:07:17,531 --> 00:07:19,318
brain of a hunter.

192
00:07:20,316 --> 00:07:23,385
Without play, many indoor cats get bored,

193
00:07:23,558 --> 00:07:25,323
stressed or overweight.

194
00:07:25,639 --> 00:07:27,846
In some surveys, more than half of

195
00:07:27,722 --> 00:07:29,696
pet cats are overweight.

196
00:07:30,653 --> 00:07:32,997
Just ten to fifteen minutes of play,

197
00:07:33,151 --> 00:07:35,104
a couple of times a day, can

198
00:07:34,943 --> 00:07:36,282
make a big difference.

199
00:07:37,248 --> 00:07:39,892
Use toys that move like prey, let

200
00:07:39,725 --> 00:07:41,309
your cat catch them at the end,

201
00:07:41,623 --> 00:07:43,960
and add shelves or cat trees so

202
00:07:43,812 --> 00:07:44,538
it can climb.

203
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:47,553
Puzzle feeders are another great idea.

204
00:07:47,877 --> 00:07:49,340
They make your cat work for its

205
00:07:49,214 --> 00:07:50,841
food, just like it would if it

206
00:07:50,687 --> 00:07:51,513
were hunting.

207
00:07:52,491 --> 00:07:54,650
Even a cardboard box or a paper

208
00:07:54,554 --> 00:07:57,117
bag can become a new adventure for

209
00:07:56,967 --> 00:07:57,986
an indoor cat.

210
00:07:58,510 --> 00:08:00,468
Fun doesn't have to be expensive.

211
00:08:01,458 --> 00:08:02,499
Myth number eleven:

212
00:08:02,948 --> 00:08:04,523
if you're pregnant, you have to give

213
00:08:04,379 --> 00:08:05,186
up your cat.

214
00:08:05,539 --> 00:08:09,625
This myth is about toxoplasmosis, an infection

215
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:11,822
that can be dangerous during pregnancy.

216
00:08:12,786 --> 00:08:14,895
Cats can spread it through their feces,

217
00:08:15,064 --> 00:08:17,225
but you're actually more likely to catch

218
00:08:17,085 --> 00:08:19,661
it from undercooked meat or soil from

219
00:08:19,492 --> 00:08:20,107
the garden.

220
00:08:21,075 --> 00:08:23,873
Doctors usually recommend simple precautions:

221
00:08:24,313 --> 00:08:25,995
let someone else clean the litter box

222
00:08:26,043 --> 00:08:29,439
every day, or use gloves and wash

223
00:08:29,306 --> 00:08:30,229
your hands well.

224
00:08:31,220 --> 00:08:33,958
Keep your cat indoors, and wash fruit

225
00:08:33,949 --> 00:08:35,022
and vegetables.

226
00:08:35,320 --> 00:08:36,274
You don't need to give up your

227
00:08:36,176 --> 00:08:36,682
cat.

228
00:08:37,006 --> 00:08:38,190
Just talk to your doctor.

229
00:08:39,155 --> 00:08:40,314
Myth number twelve:

230
00:08:40,789 --> 00:08:44,251
fish, especially tuna, is the best food

231
00:08:44,112 --> 00:08:45,000
for cats.

232
00:08:45,383 --> 00:08:47,912
Cats love the smell, but their wild

233
00:08:47,807 --> 00:08:50,490
ancestors in the desert rarely ate fish.

234
00:08:51,551 --> 00:08:53,898
Tuna made for people isn't a balanced

235
00:08:53,770 --> 00:08:56,729
diet for cats, and eating too much

236
00:08:56,581 --> 00:08:58,250
of it can cause health problems.

237
00:08:59,242 --> 00:09:01,890
Cats need complete cat food made for

238
00:09:01,739 --> 00:09:02,601
their needs.

239
00:09:02,956 --> 00:09:04,865
Tuna is fine as a tiny treat,

240
00:09:05,302 --> 00:09:06,241
not as a meal.

241
00:09:07,223 --> 00:09:09,545
The same goes for other human foods.

242
00:09:09,902 --> 00:09:13,602
Onions, garlic, chocolate and alcohol can be

243
00:09:13,484 --> 00:09:16,631
toxic to cats, and lilies are extremely

244
00:09:16,533 --> 00:09:17,437
dangerous.

245
00:09:18,409 --> 00:09:19,666
And a bonus myth:

246
00:09:20,102 --> 00:09:22,900
cats are solitary and always prefer to

247
00:09:22,752 --> 00:09:23,498
live alone.

248
00:09:23,815 --> 00:09:26,340
Many cats do enjoy their space, but

249
00:09:26,198 --> 00:09:28,476
cats can also live in friendly groups.

250
00:09:29,522 --> 00:09:33,157
Feral cats often form colonies, where related

251
00:09:33,029 --> 00:09:36,439
females share food and even help raise

252
00:09:36,298 --> 00:09:37,448
each other's kittens.

253
00:09:37,768 --> 00:09:39,627
Every cat is different.

254
00:09:40,692 --> 00:09:42,289
So, quick recap:

255
00:09:42,717 --> 00:09:45,875
no milk, use window screens, watch the

256
00:09:45,726 --> 00:09:47,951
whole cat, and remember that your cat

257
00:09:47,845 --> 00:09:49,132
really does love you.

258
00:09:50,140 --> 00:09:52,066
Play with your cat, train it with

259
00:09:51,953 --> 00:09:55,116
treats, keep tuna as a snack, and

260
00:09:54,982 --> 00:09:56,917
never believe that a black cat is

261
00:09:56,798 --> 00:09:57,641
bad luck.

262
00:09:58,626 --> 00:10:00,954
Which of these myths did you believe?

263
00:10:01,271 --> 00:10:02,955
Be honest, and tell me in the

264
00:10:02,824 --> 00:10:03,668
comments.

265
00:10:03,979 --> 00:10:05,470
I'll see you in the next video.
